From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:18:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] milkflint tests: mt76 core (mac80211.c, agg-rx, util,
 channel, scan)

10 KUnit suites. In-scope coverage:
- mac80211.c: 5.9% -> 96.1%
- agg-rx.c: 23% -> 100%
- util.c: 28% -> 100%
- channel.c: 0% -> 100%
- scan.c: 0% -> 99.3%

- mt76-core:
  - rx signal combining and rates, the CCMP header;
  - ethtool counters and page pools;
  - SAR, tx power and DFS CAC state.
- mt76-core-init:
  - phy init, the 2.4/5/6 GHz bands, stream caps and check_sband;
  - real registration with mac80211 and unregistration, for the device,
    an ext phy and a shared phy;
  - LEDs.
- mt76-core-chan: channel switching, DFS reset and survey.
- mt76-core-rx:
  - mt76_rx and A-MSDU reassembly, with the forged A-MSDU check;
  - RRO v3 and rx status conversion;
  - CCMP PN replay checks and software airtime;
  - check_sta, and poll_complete delivering frames to mac80211.
- mt76-core-sta:
  - station add/remove and events, and pre_rcu_remove;
  - wcid cleanup and polling, and reset_device;
  - keys and the offchannel notify.
- mt76-agg-rx:
  - session start, stop and shutdown;
  - in-order frames, holes, window moves and the sequence wrap at 4096;
  - BAR handling, and the reorder timer holding and releasing frames.
- mt76-util: register polls, wcid allocation edges and worker threads.
- mt76-channel: off-channel links and the end of remain-on-channel.
- mt76-scan: channel stepping and dwell times, the return to the operating
  channel, abort, probe requests and radar/no-IR beacon waits. Also a full
  scan started with iw that runs to ieee80211_scan_completed.

tests/core-hw.h, for these files only, registers the device with mac80211,
brings interfaces up with iw (a usermode helper in the VM), captures
frames on a monitor interface, and undoes it all when the test ends.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
